Keep the sleigh scanner's isatty stub to Visual C++.

The flex scanner turns off <unistd.h> on _WIN32 and defines a static
isatty() in its place. MinGW-w64 has <unistd.h>, and its <io.h>, which
the scanner includes later, declares isatty() with C linkage, so GCC and
Clang reject the stub. The stub is only needed where <unistd.h> is
missing, which is Visual C++.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/slghscan.l
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/slghscan.l
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 
 /* If we are building don't include unistd.h */
 /* flex provides us with this macro for turning it off */
-#ifdef _WIN32
+#ifdef _MSC_VER
 #define YY_NO_UNISTD_H
 static int isatty (int fildes) { return 0; }
 #endif
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/slghscan.cc
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/slghscan.cc
@@ -1140,7 +1140,7 @@
 
 /* If we are building don't include unistd.h */
 /* flex provides us with this macro for turning it off */
-#ifdef _WIN32
+#ifdef _MSC_VER
 #define YY_NO_UNISTD_H
 static int isatty (int fildes) { return 0; }
 #endif
